# Portal member login modal — design (doc-first)

```yaml
goal: Present member OTP login as a modal/sheet on portal; gate tour registration behind that modal for guests
non_goals:
  - Modalizing /catalog/{tourId}/register intake or submit
  - Writing atour_mb_session from apps/marketing
  - Deleting /login deep-link host (required for /me/* middleware gate)
  - Operator /auth/login
  - Visual redesign / CSS polish (behavior + contracts first)
```

## 1. Product contract (locked)

| Rule | Behavior |
| ---- | -------- |
| Same-page auth on portal | **Register guests** use the shared modal (desktop dialog · mobile sheet). Standalone `/login` is **page** OTP (DL-48) — the modal has no `host="login"` path. |
| Tour registration page | Full-page `/catalog/{tourId}/register` for **intake only** after member session |
| Guest on register | **PCMS-UX-MODAL-04** — auto-open login modal; **no** inline phone/OTP/profile on the page |
| Login content | phone → otp → (profile if `requires_registration`; name required, email optional) — **never** tour intake |
| Desktop | Centered dialog (`aria-modal`, focus trap, Esc closes) |
| Mobile | Bottom sheet |
| Close without success | Stay on host URL; register shows auth gate + reopen |
| Marketing | **PDP only** hosts the same OTP/profile steps in a marketing modal via Portal-origin transport (stay on `/tours/{id}`). Guest «ثبت‌نام» and «ورود» both open that modal (Phase 6). **Header Sign in** navigates to Portal `/login` (page OTP). No Marketing BFF. Future marketing login hosts may reuse the PDP modal. |
| Shared auth steps | `GuestAuthTransport` + host `onAuthenticated` — no BFF URLs or intake hydrate in OTP/profile UI |

## 2. Why marketing SSR already detects portal members

PCMS-001 already requires marketing **read-only** detection of `atour_mb_session` for header chrome:

| Layer | File | Role |
| ----- | ---- | ---- |
| Cookie read | `apps/marketing/src/auth/read-marketing-member-session.server.ts` | `cookies()` + raw `Cookie` → `validateSessionTokenAsync` |
| Header resolve | `apps/marketing/src/shell/resolve-marketing-member-header.server.ts` | Tenant bind + `GET /identity/me` for display/avatar |
| Shell | `apps/marketing/src/shell/marketing-shell.tsx` | Guest: `data-marketing-header-sign-in` · Member: `data-marketing-header-member` |

**Cross-surface cookie sharing (must remain true after modal):**

1. Auth BFF writes **host-only** cookie on portal ingress (PCMS-COOK-02).
2. Next portal request (including `waitForMemberSessionCookie` → `GET /api/me/profile`) commits the session; on **custom apex**, middleware refreshes `Domain=<registrable-apex>` (PCMS-COOK-03 / COOK-01).
3. Cross-surface marketing header chrome requires apex hosts (`denali.club` ↔ `portal.denali.club`). `*.localhost` stays host-only — marketing cannot read the portal cookie.
4. Marketing SSR on next page load (apex) shows profile chip instead of Sign in.

**Design invariant PCMS-UX-MODAL-COOKIE:** Modal success paths **must** run `waitForMemberSessionCookie()` (or equivalent same-origin authenticated probe) before considering login complete — even when staying on the register page — so the cookie is committed and apex COOK-03 can share with marketing SSR.

**Bounded probe (anti-hang):** `waitForMemberSessionCookie` must not wait forever on a hung `/api/me/profile` BFF (first compile / overloaded Next). Each attempt uses a short `AbortSignal` timeout; after a finite attempt budget the probe returns `false` and the OTP step surfaces a localized network error instead of leaving the UI stuck on «در حال تأیید…». Navigation (`location.assign(portalReturn)`) only runs after a successful probe.

## 3. Host matrix

| Host page | How modal opens | After OTP success |
| --------- | --------------- | ----------------- |
| `/catalog/{id}/register` | **Auto for guests** (PCMS-UX-MODAL-04); `?auth=login` compatible; reopen via Sign-in control | Close modal · **stay** · resume/hydrate **intake-only** (PCMS-REG-01) |
| `/login` (thin public host) | Auto-open on load | `waitForMemberSessionCookie` then `location.assign(portalReturn)` |
| Protected `/me/*` | **Cannot** host modal for guests | Middleware → `/login?portalReturn=<path>` (unchanged) |
| Marketing header Sign in | **Navigate** to Portal `/login?portalReturn=/me/registrations` — not the marketing modal | Portal **page** OTP, then `portalReturn` |
| Marketing PDP `/tours/{id}` | Guest `[data-marketing-register]` and `[data-marketing-tour-sign-in]` client-open marketing modal; optional `?auth=login` auto-open **only** on this pathname | Origin `probeSession` then **reload current PDP URL** |

**Closed-modal a11y (2026-08-07):** `PortalLoginModalProvider` must not leave a visible/AT-exposed «ورود» / Sign-in `h2` on authenticated pages. When `open=false`, dialog content is unmounted and the `<dialog>` is `inert` so screen readers and a11y snapshots do not see a ghost login heading under `/me/*`.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  subgraph marketing [Marketing]
    MKT_READ[readMarketingMemberSessionFromCookies]
    MKT_HEADER[Header Sign in]
    MKT_PDP[PDP guest register / ورود]
    MKT_MEMBER[Profile chip]
    MKT_MODAL[Marketing login modal]
    MKT_READ -->|null| MKT_HEADER
    MKT_READ -->|null| MKT_PDP
    MKT_READ -->|valid + tenant bind| MKT_MEMBER
    MKT_PDP -->|JS + portal origin| MKT_MODAL
    MKT_MODAL -->|CORS public-auth + reload PDP| MKT_READ
  end

  subgraph portal [Portal]
    REG["/catalog/id/register PAGE"]
    LOGIN["/login page OTP"]
    MODAL[Register-only login modal dialog/sheet]
    GATE[Guest auth gate — no inline OTP]
    ME["/me/*"]
    REG -->|guest| GATE
    GATE -->|auto-open| MODAL
    LOGIN -->|onAuthenticated| ME
    ME -->|guest middleware| LOGIN
    MODAL -->|success on register| INTAKE[intake-only on REG]
  end

  MKT_HEADER --> LOGIN
  MKT_PDP -->|no-JS / no origin| REG
```

## 4. URL builders (target contract)

| Actor | Builder (keep / adjust) | Target URL after this design |
| ----- | ----------------------- | ---------------------------- |
| Marketing header Sign in | `resolvePortalMemberLoginUrl` | **Primary:** Portal `/login?portalReturn=/me/registrations` (page OTP). Not the marketing modal. |
| Marketing tour «ورود» | `resolvePortalRegistrationLoginUrl` | **Primary:** marketing modal on PDP (stay on `/tours/{id}` after reload). **Fallback href:** `{portal}/catalog/{tourId}/register?auth=login` |
| Marketing tour guest «ثبت‌نام» | `resolvePortalRegistrationUrl` | **Primary:** marketing modal on PDP (same trigger). **Fallback href (no-JS):** `{portal}/catalog/{tourId}/register` |
| Portal register «ورود» | client open modal | Same URL; optional `?auth=login` for shareable deep link |
| Middleware `/me` guest | `resolvePortalMemberLoginPath` | `/login?portalReturn=<requested path>` |

**Query `auth=login`:**

- Allowed on **public** portal routes that may host the modal (register; optionally future public hubs).
- On **marketing**, auto-open is allowed **only** on a tour-detail pathname (`/tours/{id}` or `/en/tours/{id}`). Home, `/tours` list, and other marketing routes ignore `?auth=login` so header Sign in stays a Portal `/login` navigation.
- Ignored when session already valid → SSR/client goes intake-only / no modal (PCMS-UX-02 spirit).
- Safe parsing: exact `auth=login` (no open redirect). `portalReturn` remains the return contract for `/login` host only (DL-12).

## 5. Component architecture

```text
apps/portal
  PortalProviders
    PortalLoginModalProvider          ← client context: open/close, portalReturn?, presentation
      dialog/sheet
        PublicCatalogRegistrationFlow
          GuestAuthHostProvider       ← transport + host onAuthenticated
            shared phone / otp / profile steps
  app/login/page.tsx
    PortalLoginThinHost               ← page OTP · data-portal-login-full-page + form-panel
    onAuthenticated → completeMemberLoginEgress (portalReturn)
    smoke tourId = flow plugin bootstrap only (no intake, no 404)
```

| Piece | Responsibility |
| ----- | -------------- |
| `PortalLoginModalProvider` | Register-only `openLoginModal({ flow, portalReturn? })`. Always `data-portal-login-modal-host="register"`. Close + reload. **Zero** `completeMemberLoginEgress`. |
| `PublicCatalogRegistrationFlow` | Portal host shell: injects Portal same-origin transport + `onAuthenticated`; SSR-stable `memberLoginEgress` |
| `/login/page.tsx` | Public SSR host: PCMS-UX-01/02 gates · `data-portal-return` · `data-portal-login-full-page`. **Inline** phone/OTP/profile. Smoke `tourId` is flow-plugin bootstrap only (missing catalog row must not 404). |
| `PortalLoginThinHost` | Client page host: story panel + `[data-portal-login-form-panel]` mounting `PublicCatalogRegistrationFlow` (`memberLoginEgress`). **Zero** `openLoginModal`. |
| Page-host `onAuthenticated` | `completeMemberLoginEgress({ memberLoginEgress: true })` (**no** second cookie probe — steps already `probeSession`). Register host stays close + reload. |
| Register page | Session → intake flow. Guest → auth gate + auto modal (PCMS-UX-MODAL-04); reopen via Sign-in · `?auth=login` compatible |
| `@app-tour/catalog-registration-flow-ui` `GuestAuthTransport` | Phone/OTP/profile **network + session probe** only. Portal factory: same-origin `/api/public-auth/*` + `GET /api/me/profile`. Marketing factory: absolute portal `/api/public-auth/*` + `GET {origin}/api/public-auth/session`. No cookie write, no tenant, no intake. |
| `GuestAuthHostProvider` | Injects `{ transport, onAuthenticated }` into auth steps. Steps throw if mounted outside the provider. |
| Host `onAuthenticated` | Login: `completeMemberLoginEgress`. Register modal: close + reload register URL. **Marketing modal:** reload current marketing URL. Portal register resume (non-login-egress): `hydrateCatalogRegistrationIntakeAfterSession` on the **flow host**, never inside OTP/profile steps. |
| Marketing | Phase 5/6: `MarketingLoginModalProvider` in layout (needed for PDP). Trigger is **PDP-only** (`[data-marketing-tour-sign-in]` + guest `[data-marketing-register]`). Header Sign in is a plain GSH `/login` `<a>`. Hooks `data-marketing-login-modal*`. No `PublicCatalogRegistrationFlow`. No marketing public-auth BFF. Phase 4 CORS remains Portal `/api/public-auth/*` only. |

**Presentation hooks (stable for smoke/CSS):**

| Hook | Meaning |
| ---- | ------- |
| `data-portal-login-modal` | Modal root |
| `data-portal-login-modal-open` | Open state |
| `data-portal-login-modal-presentation="dialog"\|"sheet"` | Desktop vs mobile |
| `data-portal-login-modal-host="register"` | Register-route modal only (DL-48 deleted `host="login"`) |
| Keep | `data-member-login-egress`, `data-portal-return`, phone/otp hooks |

## 6. Egress modes (unchanged semantics, new presentation)

| Mode | When | Post-cookie |
| ---- | ---- | ----------- |
| **Login host egress** | **Page** on `/login` (not the modal) | `probeSession` then page-host `onAuthenticated` → `completeMemberLoginEgress` / `location.assign(portalReturn)` |
| **Register-host login** | Modal on register (required for guests; **only** remaining portal modal host) | `probeSession` → host `onAuthenticated` (close modal → reload / SSR resume intake-only) — **forbid** intake inside modal or OTP steps. Modal must not import `completeMemberLoginEgress`. |
| **Guest inline register auth** | — | **Removed** (PCMS-UX-MODAL-04) |

`memberLoginEgress` prop remains SSR-stable for modal body. Register-host login uses a distinct success handler (not intake-inside-modal).

## 7. Marketing SSR after portal login — sequence

```text
1. Guest on marketing → Sign in / tour ورود
2. JS: marketing modal · origin fetch Portal `/api/public-auth/*` (CORS)
   no-JS: land on portal (`/login` page OTP or register?auth=login → register modal)
3. OTP success → Set-Cookie (Portal BFF) → origin probe GET `/api/public-auth/session`
4. Marketing reloads current URL. On custom apex, COOK-03 `Domain=<apex>` lets SSR see the cookie
5. Header shows profile chip (data-marketing-header-member); PDP CTA matrix hides tour sign-in
```

**Failure modes to design against:**

| Failure | Symptom | Guard |
| ------- | ------- | ----- |
| Skip cookie probe | Marketing still shows Sign in | PCMS-UX-MODAL-COOKIE + UX-03 |
| Tenant mismatch | Header null | `sessionTenantMatchesDevCrossSurfaceHost` |
| Host-only on *.localhost / missing apex Domain | Marketing still Sign in | Use custom apex hosts; COOK-03 apex refresh |

## 8. `/login` retention rationale

| Question | Answer |
| -------- | ------ |
| Can we delete `/login`? | **No** — `/me/*` is middleware-gated; guests never get a React tree to mount a modal on |
| Is `/login` still a “big page”? | **Yes for OTP chrome (DL-48)** — story + `[data-portal-login-form-panel]`. It is not the register modal. |
| Standalone bookmark login? | Yes — `/login` with default `portalReturn` |

## 9. Accessibility & responsive

Portal `/login` page and `data-portal-login-modal` keep the contracts below. **Marketing PDP** `[data-marketing-login-modal]` is a separate Quiet Ledger skin (`37-mkt-login-modal.css`) — do not restyle Portal chrome to match it.

| Viewport | Pattern | Notes |
| -------- | ------- | ----- |
| `min-width` desktop breakpoint (align Denali portal shell) | Centered dialog | Focus trap · Esc · backdrop click optional (product: prefer Esc + close button) |
| Below breakpoint | Bottom sheet | Portal register modal may keep a close control. **Marketing auth bridge:** no drag handle, no swipe-dismiss (in-progress OTP must not be discarded by a gesture). `env(safe-area-inset-bottom)` + `--kb-inset` from `visualViewport`. |
| Both | `aria-modal="true"` · labelled by login title · restore focus to trigger |
| Marketing bridge only | Dismiss | Escape + visible Cancel (`loginModalCancel`). Backdrop click is ignored. First focus is the phone field or OTP cell 0, not Close. |

## 10. Theme / CSS

- Extend `packages/workspaces/denali/theme/portal/login-page.css` with `[data-portal-login-modal]` — do **not** reuse `main[data-portal-member-login-page] { min-height: 100dvh }` on the modal panel.
- **Dialog centering (required):** Tailwind / Preflight resets native `<dialog>` `margin: auto`, so an open modal collapses to the top-inline-start corner (top-right under RTL). Denali skin must re-center with a full-viewport flex frame on `[data-portal-login-modal][open]` / `[data-portal-login-modal-open="true"]`:
  - Desktop (`presentation="dialog"`): `display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; inset/width/height cover viewport; margin: 0; transparent surface`.
  - Mobile sheet (`presentation="sheet"`): same frame with `align-items: flex-end` so the panel docks to the bottom safe area.
  - Panel keeps `width: min(100vw - 2rem, 28rem)` (dialog) / full bleed (sheet); do **not** rely on UA dialog margin alone.
- Register-host modal: hide gate chrome while the modal is open (`body:has([data-portal-login-modal-open="true"])`). `/login` no longer uses host-lede (page form).
- Guest gate (PCMS-UX-MODAL-04): `[data-portal-register-guest-auth]` · `[data-portal-register-auth-gate]` · primary `[data-portal-register-sign-in-button]` — muted while modal open.
- Modal OTP controls: `denali-form-controls.css` scopes `[data-portal-login-modal-body]` alongside `[data-portal-auth-card]`.
- **No registration stepper** inside the login modal (`memberLoginEgress` skips `CatalogRegistrationStepper`); modal header title is the only step chrome.
- Register page full-viewport auth experience **unchanged** when modal closed.
- `/login` page uses the existing `data-portal-login-full-page` alpine skin (story + form panel).

